  "content": {
    "body": "`pebbles-cli map` builds and saves a TRUE dependency graph of the\nproject — not a file list. 28 languages, each language's matcher\nmaintained as its own module plugged into one central engine; honors\n`.pebblesignore` (gitignore syntax at the project root — exclude\nvendor/, storage/, lockfiles, .env). NO FILE CAP — the entire project\nis mapped, however long it takes (completeness beats speed); `--max`\nexists only as an optional user bound, and the summary's `truncated`\nflag can only appear when one was passed.\n\n## What the mapper extracts\n\n- Symbols per file with line + kind (class, function, interface, …).\n- Typed edges: import · dynamic-import · re-export · extends ·\n  implements · mixin — resolved through tiers (relative path →\n  full-spec symbol → filename → NAMESPACE PATH (the spec's segment\n  chain matched against file paths, PSR-4 style — disambiguates\n  same-named classes in different namespaces) → last-segment → stem)\n  with a fanout guard against ambiguous matches.\n- CALL edges: call sites attributed to their ENCLOSING function and\n  disambiguated through each caller's imports — so map-callers answers\n  \"who actually invokes this,\" not \"where does this string appear.\"\n- Hubs: files ranked by in-degree (most imported). Hubs approximate the\n  domain core — extraction and audits start there.\n\n## Queries (token-cheap slices; never dump the whole graph)\n\n- `map [--fresh] [--max N]` — (re)build + save; prints a summary\n  (files, byLanguage, edge counts, hubs, truncation notice if any).\n- `map-symbol <name> [--kind K]` — definition sites.\n  `pebbles-cli map-symbol ServiceRequest --kind class`\n- `map-file <path>` — one file's symbols, imports, imported-by, calls,\n  AND the reverse join: `pebbles` lists every spec pebble whose\n  codeLinks bind this file — \"what governs this code?\" in one call.\n  THE fastest analysis entry point; accepts a pebble's codeLink path.\n- `map-search <term> [--max N] [--kind K]` — relevance-ranked matches\n  (exact symbol > symbol prefix > filename > path; camelCase/snake_case\n  token-aware, so \"workorder\" finds createWorkOrder), in-degree as the\n  tie-breaker.\n- `map-neighbors <path> [--in|--out] [--depth N]` — dependency\n  closure: --in = who depends on it, --out = what it pulls in.\n- `map-callers <symbol>` — every call site with the calling function.\n\n## Freshness\n\nQueries read the latest SAVED run; the chat relay reports its age and\nfile count (\"PROJECT MAP STATUS … use --fresh if the code has changed\",\nor \"NO MAP YET — run map first\"). Extraction REQUIRES a current map.\nSaved runs live under .pebbles/.maps/<timestamp>/ (local, not spec).\n\n## Spec ↔ map binding\n\nA pebble's `codeLinks[].path` doubles as a map node id: `map-file` on\nit yields that file's full graph context instantly. The audit skill\nre-checks every codeLink against a fresh map (file gone → status\nmissing; symbol gone → drift) so the spec can't silently rot.\n\n## Navigation doctrine\n\nLocate code through the map, not grep: definition → map-symbol ·\nfeature → map-search · context → map-file · blast radius →\nmap-neighbors --in + map-callers. Only read the files the graph points\nyou to.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
